1. Data Modeling: Star Schema
Fact Table (FactSales): Stores transaction-level numerical metrics (quantity, price, LineTotal) and key IDs (invoice, stockcode, customerid, invoicedate).

Dimension Tables (DimDate, DimProduct, DimCustomer): Store unique lookup attributes (dates, descriptions, customer locations).

Relationships: Configured as 1-to-Many (1:*) single-direction links from Dimensions to the Fact table for efficient filtering and fast report performance.

2. ETL & Data Preparation (Power Query)
Data Cleansing: Filtered out negative quantities and cancellation invoices (starting with "C"), and handled missing customerid entries.

Feature Engineering: Added a calculated column (LineTotal = quantity * price) in Power Query to reduce DAX memory overhead during runtime.

Data Type Optimization: Explicitly set data types (Date, Decimal Number, Text) to prevent implicit conversions and model errors.

3. Analytics & Logic (DAX)
Aggregation: Computed core metrics using SUM and SUMX.

Distinct Counting: Used DISTINCTCOUNT(invoice) to count unique orders rather than individual transaction rows.

Safe Division: Applied DIVIDE(Numerator, Denominator, 0) for Average Order Value (AOV) to prevent divide-by-zero errors.

Time Intelligence: Built dynamic Month-over-Month (MoM) growth calculations using CALCULATE, DATEADD, and MONTH functions referenced against a dedicated date calendar table (DimDate).

4. Interactive Data Visualization
High-Level KPIs: Multi-card visual layout showcasing Total Revenue, Total Orders, Average Order Value, and Total Customers.

Time Series Trend Analysis: Line charts displaying revenue progression over time.
Ranking & Top-N Analysis: Horizontal bar charts filtered to isolate top-performing products by revenue.

Geographic & Customer Segmentation: Maps and matrix visual tables paired with cross-filtering slicers (Year, Month, Country) for multi-dimensional drill-downs.
